window.OPOSSUM_FOOT_LEGAL_HTML = "<h3>Who owns this</h3>\n<p>Opossum Foot — the app, the name, the logo, the design, and everything in it — is the property of <strong>Opossum Foot LLC</strong>, an Iowa limited liability company. Copyright © 2026 Opossum Foot LLC. All rights reserved.</p>\n<h3>Closed beta — keep it in the circle</h3>\n<p>You're using a closed beta, and the circle is small on purpose. Please don't share the beta link, copy the app, or pull it apart to build your own version of it. If someone wants in, point them at Tanner.</p>\n<h3>No warranties</h3>\n<p>The app is provided as-is. It was built to be solid, but no software is perfect — Opossum Foot LLC isn't responsible for anything that goes wrong because of a glitch. Back up your data in Settings — the full JSON backup is the one that restores everything; the CSV exports are your spreadsheet copies.</p>\n<h3>Seasons are reminders, not law</h3>\n<p>Season dates, bag limits, and everything else in the Seasons tab are reminders only — <strong>not legal authority</strong>. Always verify with your state agency and local ordinances before you trap. Nothing in this app decides whether trapping is legal today.</p>\n<h3>About the Information in This App</h3>\n<p>Opossum Foot is a pocket notebook and reference tool. It is not a law book, not a field guide, and not a substitute for either.</p>\n<p><strong>Regulations and seasons.</strong> The season dates, zones, limits, and regulation notes in this app are summaries prepared for quick reference — the same way the printed regulations booklet in your truck is a summary. They are not complete, they are not the law, and they can be wrong: agencies set and change seasons every year, sometimes mid-season, and a summary can lag behind or miss a change. The official publications and websites of each state's fish and wildlife agency, and the state code itself, are the only authorities. Before you set a trap, hunt, or travel to trap somewhere new, verify the current rules with that state's agency. A season reminder or an \"open\" flag in this app is a nudge to check — it is never permission. You are solely responsible for knowing and obeying the laws and regulations everywhere you trap, and for holding the licenses, permits, and tags those laws require.</p>\n<p>Opossum Foot carries the most recent regulations and rules each state has published. States publish on their own schedules, and some publish later than others. Where a state's current guide has not yet been published, the app shows the latest information that state has released and marks it as such — when the state publishes, the app is updated. The state's current official publication is always the authority.</p>\n<p><strong>Sign, plants, and fungi.</strong> The sign and forage information in this app is educational, and it is written for identification by sight. It is not a foraging guide. Identifications can be wrong — including any you record yourself with the app's markers — and some wild plants and fungi have poisonous look-alikes. Never eat, use, or feed to any person or animal any wild plant or fungus based on anything in this app. Confirm any identification in person with a qualified local expert.</p>\n<p><strong>Maps, GPS, and land.</strong> Maps, satellite imagery, GPS positions, routes, and any boundary or landowner information in this app are approximate. They may be out of date, misaligned, or wrong, and they are not a legal survey. Nothing in this app gives you the right to enter any land. Obey posted signs, and get the landowner's permission before you set foot — let alone a trap — on private ground. You are responsible for knowing whose land you are on at all times.</p>\n<p><strong>Your responsibility; no warranty; limits.</strong> Trapping and time outdoors carry inherent risks — weather, terrain, water, animals, and equipment among them. You assume those risks, and responsibility for your own decisions and actions in the field. This app is provided \"as is\" and \"as available,\" without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including accuracy, completeness, or fitness for a particular purpose. Nothing in this app is legal advice. To the maximum extent permitted by law, Opossum Foot LLC will not be liable for any fines, citations, injuries, losses, or damages — direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential — arising from your use of or reliance on this app or its information. If anything in this app ever conflicts with an official source, the official source governs.</p>\n<h3>The fine print, plainly</h3>\n<p>This isn't legal advice, and it isn't the full terms of service — those are coming. By using the beta, you agree to use it legally and to keep the beta link to yourself.</p>";
